# Lab red-team policy (Cybersec Phase-1)

Adversarial LLM / agent eval tools are **authorized lab only**. No LIVE Discord, no unauthorized targets.

## Authorization

- Written scope (owned lab, bug-bounty rules, or engagement letter) before running FuzzyAI, AHA, cryptex, Senthex, OpenART/EMHA, PIMiner, ARIA instruction-backdoor RT, Trident-class DRL red, ILL inaudible-LF audio, Taboo decoding-time diagnostic, or similar.
- OpenART (`raw-sources/repos/OpenART`) is **AGPL-3.0** — lab sandbox only; do not network-serve or ship into prod without license review.
- Prefer Docker-sandboxed victims; never point autoresearch red-team loops at third-party production.
- Kid-safety / social-engineering pages are for parent/teacher/LE context — not offensive grooming research.
- AirKey-class Wi-Fi CSI + acoustic PIN inference: **authorized physical/wireless lab only** — no LIVE/unauthorized eavesdrop.

## Eval discipline

- Report dual metrics where relevant (overall ASR vs full/phase ASR); do not optimize a single ASR number.
- Respect evidential ceilings — stop claiming more certainty than the eval design supports (`ai-redteam-evidential-limits`).
- InferScale / KV-injection: treat shared-prefix or cache-poison findings as security bugs in agent infra, not as free speedups to ship unchecked.

## Training data / fine-tune

- Run DataShield-class risky-finetune filters in lab before any Cemini/TipDrop fine-tune on scraped corpora.
- Do **not** install OC-GRPO or other GRPO trainer stacks as “wired” harness — REFERENCE/paper repro only.
- Notes-to-self / experiential memory clones: lab only; reconstruct before inject (see federation MemHarness rule).

